-11", "authorid": 831, "bench": [831], "title": "Omkarnath S. Parashar vs State Of Gujarat And Anr. on 11 October, 2005", "numcites": 26, "numcitedby": 5, "headline": "lodged for an offence under  <b>Section</b> 44  of <b>Electricity</b> Act read with  <b>Section</b> 379  of the IPC. The petitioner had deposited entire amount of impugned ... Board and there was no specific provision of <b>compounding</b> of offence. Now  <b>Section</b> <b>152</b>  of the <b>Electricity</b> Act specifically makes the said provision", "docsize": 34925, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Gujarat High Court", "author": "K A Puj", "authorEncoded": "k-a-puj", "citation": "(2006)2GLR1056"}, {"tid": 107870801, "catids": [4], "doctype": 1024, "publishdate": "2021-01-19", "authorid": null, "bench": null, "title": "Amit Kumar vs State Of Punjab And Another on 19 January, 2021", "numcites": 8, "numcitedby": 3, "headline": "<b>Section</b> 135  of the <b>Electricity</b> Act, 2003 defines and\n\npenalises theft of <b>electricity</b> while  <b>Section</b> <b>152</b>  of the <b>Electricity</b> Act,\n\n2003 makes the same <b>compoundable</b> ... under sub-<b>section</b> (1)\n            shall be allowed only once for any person or consumer.&quot;\n \n             The provisions of  <b>Section</b> <b>152</b>  of the <b>Electricity</b>", "docsize": 36284, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Punjab-Haryana High Court"}, {"tid": 108078507, "catids": [424], "doctype": 1008, "publishdate": "2013-12-04", "authorid": 1703, "bench": [1703], "title": "M/S Torrent Power Ltd. vs The State Of U.P. Thru Secy. And Others on 4 December, 2013", "numcites": 12, "numcitedby": 3, "headline": "provision of  <b>Section</b> 126  read with  <b>Section</b> 135  of the <b>Electricity</b> Act, it is apparently clear, that usage of <b>electricity</b> for the purposes other than ... <b>Electricity</b> Act provides for <b>compounding</b> of certain offences. For facility,  <b>Section</b> <b>152</b>  is extracted hereunder:\n  \n \t&quot;<b>152</b>. <b>Compounding</b> of offences.- (1) Notwithstanding anything contained", "docsize": 27469, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Allahabad High Court", "author": "T Agarwala", "authorEncoded": "t-agarwala"}, {"tid": 1321814, "catids": [10, 612, 175], "doctype": 1022, "publishdate": "2007-04-27", "authorid": 1551, "bench": [1551], "title": "K.N. Ram @ Kedar Nath Ram vs The State Of Bihar And Anr. on 27 April, 2007", "numcites": 9, "numcitedby": 3, "headline": "connection attention has been drawn towards  <b>Section</b> <b>152</b>  of the Indian <b>Electricity</b> Act which lays down as follows:\n   \n\n <b>152</b>(2); On payment ... amount has been accepted and there is Statutory <b>compounding</b> of offence under  <b>Section</b> <b>152</b>  of the <b>Electricity</b> Act, which has not been rebutted on behalf", "docsize": 10782, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Patna High Court", "author": "S Mukherjee", "authorEncoded": "s-mukherjee"}, {"tid": 46649992, "catids": null, "doctype": 1003, "publishdate": "2021-03-17", "authorid": 634, "bench": [634], "title": "Sanjeev Dua vs State & Anr on 17 March, 2021", "numcites": 10, "numcitedby": 3, "headline": "offence punishable under  <b>Section</b> 135  of the Indian\n<b>Electricity</b> Act, 2003 is <b>compoundable</b> in terms of  <b>Section</b> <b>152</b>  of the said\nenactment, in view", "docsize": 6901, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Delhi High Court - Orders", "author": "A Malhotra", "authorEncoded": "a-malhotra"}, {"tid": 136765559, "catids": [424], "doctype": 1002, "publishdate": "2020-06-30", "authorid": 635, "bench": [635], "title": "Tata Power Delhi Distribution Limited vs Rampal on 30 June, 2020", "numcites": 46, "numcitedby": 1, "headline": " Tata Power Delhi Distribution Limited vs Rampal on 30 June, 2020 \n\n Equivalent citations: AIRONLINE 2020", "docsize": 110443, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Delhi High Court", "author": "A J Bhambani", "authorEncoded": "a-j-bhambani", "citation": "AIRONLINE 2020 D